    "narrative": "The offensive core for LawDog today centers on **Will Smith** and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who represent our highest floor and ceiling combinations. **Will Smith** draws a favorable matchup against Lodolo (4.71 xERA), and his performance is bolstered significantly by his high-leverage slot in the #3 hole and solid xwOBA peripherals. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a must-start despite facing a left-hander; his elite talent level overrides the platoon disadvantage, and his #2 position provides the volume necessary to remain in our high-60s efficiency tier. **Dylan Beavers** also emerges as a high-upside play today, capitalizing on an ideal #1 order spot against Tong; his sprint speed remains a vital asset for our scarce SB category, and the matchup profile suggests he will see high-quality pitches in a favorable run-scoring environment.\n\nOur bench decision was anchored by **Braden Montgomery**, who narrowly missed the cut with a score of 32.65. While his profile often provides pop, the combination of facing an elite arm in Williams (2.89 xERA) and the reduced opportunity inherent in a #9 order slot kept him below our mandatory 40.0 efficiency threshold. Conversely, we are playing it safe with **JJ Bleday** today; despite his 44.84 score\u2014largely driven by a platoon advantage\u2014he faces a daunting matchup against Skubal (2.84 xERA). We are essentially betting on **JJ Bleday** to navigate a tough southpaw assignment through efficiency, but he remains the most volatile piece of our starting rotation today. We will continue to monitor the status of **Bryce Harper**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Justin Crawford** for upcoming series, as their absence from today\u2019s schedule significantly limits our flexibility to pivot if any of our starters\u2014particularly **Cal Raleigh** or **Gleyber Torres**\u2014face mid-game defensive substitutions or weather delays.",
